  "notes": "Composed of {交|こう} (intersect, exchange) and {尾|び} (tail). Literally \"crossing tails.\" A scientific, neutral term used exclusively for animals — never for humans in standard usage. Common in biology textbooks, nature documentaries, and wildlife observation contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {交尾|こうび}する: to mate\n- {交尾|こうび}の{時期|じき}: mating season\n- {交尾|こうび}{行動|こうどう}: mating behavior\n- {交尾|こうび}{相手|あいて}: mating partner\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- つがい: mating pair — refers to a bonded pair of animals, often birds\n- {繁殖|はんしょく}: breeding, reproduction — broader term covering the whole reproductive process including raising young\n- {生殖|せいしょく}: reproduction — the biological process; more technical and scientific",
